Why There Are No Discounts, No Trials, and Why the Price Will Keep Rising (September 13, 2026)

I don’t offer discounts or free trials. Not because I’m trying to be difficult. Because I don’t need your money. My daily or weekly swings in my portfolios are larger than what the paid subscription would earn me over 120 years. So if you’re wondering why I still charge, the answer is simple: price is a filter.

Lazy people stay poor because they look for shortcuts. They want the result without the work, the signal without the discipline, the tip without the process. Serious people understand that wealth is built by doing more than most people are willing to do, for longer than most people are willing to stay. I never consider myself rich by my own Hong Kong standard. That is why I still work, still chart, still refine. I enjoy it. I would do it anyway. I work harder than most because I sincerely want everyone to succeed and outperform in this cycle. No other content creator spends more than 35 hours during the weekend analyzing, charting, working, and making videos for the community and most hide behind the excuse that weekends are for relaxation and family gatherings.

I will definitely keep raising the tier prices.  Plenty of $200 to $2,000 monthly subscriptions still fail at the only job that matters this cycle: pointing to the right core stocks and helping you hold them with the right size. Price without quality is a tax. Quality without a serious price just attracts tourists. I charge for quality, quantity, accuracy, and a record that can be checked. Nobody else does what Dr Cat @cantonmeow  and I have been doing consistently: sharing 50–70 tickers for analysis and more than 50 weekly videos at an affordable rate—about the price of a simple dinner in Hong Kong, and half the price of a Chinese dinner for two at normal Chinese restaurants. That is enough reason to raise the fee.

My Patreon is not for tourists hunting pocket money. It is not for people who want a lottery ticket dressed up as a strategy. It is for people who want to build serious wealth by concentrating in the right core holdings and keeping speculative positions small. I know almost everyone here thinks like a trader and the majority are traders on X. I chose the opposite. I am a genuine long-term investor (at least for a cycle of 3 to 10 years). The screenshots, the messages, and the record are there for anyone who actually looks. I don’t need to brag. I also don’t need to pretend that wealth is made in a month or even a year. If you are serious, you think in cycles of 3 to 10 years. You put real weight in a few core names and keep the speculative positions small.

The price exists to protect that process. It keeps out the person who will leave at the first drawdown and end up missing the bull trend later. It keeps in the person who understands that the edge is not a hot idea, but staying with the right stocks through a full cycle is what creates wealth. It buys more work, not more noise. It makes the room smaller, sharper, and less crowded with people who never intended to hold the right stocks in the bull cycle.

If you want a cheap feed of trades, this is the wrong place. If you want a long path in the core holdings that actually matter this cycle, with discipline around size and time, then the door is priced that way on purpose.
I will keep working. I will keep charting. I will keep raising both the standard and the fee. The market does not negotiate. Neither do I.

